1.Privacy and Data Protection

OptiTutor is an educational AI assistant designed for students studying optics and optometry.

Students should not enter personal information, passwords, medical records or other sensitive data into the chat.

The application does not require students to provide personal information to ask educational questions. However, users should be aware that messages are processed by an external AI service through the n8n workflow.

The assistant should only be used for educational purposes.

2. Bias and Fairness

AI models may generate biased, incomplete or inaccurate information because of limitations in their training data and language-generation processes.

OptiTutor aims to provide clear and accessible explanations for all students, regardless of their level of prior knowledge.

However, the quality of answers may vary depending on how questions are formulated and the language used.

Teachers should supervise its use and encourage students to compare AI-generated information with reliable educational sources.

3. Transparency

Students must be informed that OptiTutor is an artificial intelligence assistant and not a human teacher or healthcare professional.

Its responses are generated automatically by an AI language model and may contain errors.

The system should be presented as a learning support tool rather than an authoritative source of information.

4. Accountability and Safety

OptiTutor is designed to explain educational concepts related to optics, optometry and contact lenses.

It must not provide medical diagnoses, prescribe medication or recommend treatments.

When students describe symptoms such as eye pain, redness or blurred vision, the assistant should avoid medical recommendations and advise them to contact an appropriate healthcare professional.

Teachers remain responsible for supervising the educational use of the assistant and checking the accuracy of its content.

5. Ethical Conclusion

OptiTutor demonstrates how artificial intelligence can support education when used responsibly.

Its main purpose is to encourage learning, curiosity and independent study.

Human supervision, transparency, privacy awareness and critical evaluation of AI-generated information are essential to its responsible use.
